    "body": "<!-- markdownlint-disable -->\r\n## Purpose\r\n\r\nAdds `longcat_next` to two `model_type` allowlists in vLLM core that currently only recognize `\"longcat_flash\"`/`\"longcat_flash_ngram\"`. LongCat-Next reuses that backbone (`FlashNgramModel`, `FlashDecoderLayer`) unchanged, but ships under a different `model_type` string, so it falls through both checks today.\r\n\r\n- **`gpu_model_runner.py` / `gpu/attn_utils.py`** — `num_attn_module` selection for `bind_kv_cache`'s layer-index parsing. LongCat's decoder layers have two MLA `Attention` modules per layer (e.g. `model.layers.0.self_attn.0.attn`), which needs `num_attn_module=2`.\r\n  - Without it: `AssertionError: layer name ... should only contain one integer`\r\n- **`model_arch_config_convertor.py`** — `is_deepseek_mla()`'s allowlist, which decides whether `get_head_size()` uses `kv_lora_rank + qk_rope_head_dim` (576, correct) or falls back to `hidden_size // num_attention_heads` (96, wrong).\r\n  - Without it: `ValueError: Head dimension 96 is not supported by MLA.`\r\n\r\nLongCat-Next's model/processor live in vLLM-Omni (integrated via the omni runner's `preprocess()` hook, not vLLM's native V2-runner ngram path), so this PR is scoped to just these two allowlists — no new files.\r\n\r\nCompanion PR (depends on this): vllm-project/vllm-omni#5299 \r\n\r\n## Test Plan\r\n\r\n- Unit: isolated checks against the real checkpoint (`meituan-longcat/LongCat-Next`) confirming `is_deepseek_mla()` → 576 and `num_attn_module=2` resolves the dual-attention layer names.\r\n- E2E: 4×A100-40GB, TP=4, fp8 quantization, via the companion PR's deploy config — live server, 3 chat-completion requests (text/image/audio).\r\n\r\n## Test Result\r\n\r\n- E2E: all 3 requests succeeded (`finish_reason: stop`, no errors). Server healthy in ~5 min (74B/15-shard checkpoint, fp8).\r\n- Not covered: generation-side stages, TP configs other than 4, CUDA graphs (`enforce_eager=True` throughout).\r\n\r\n---\r\n<details>\r\n<summary>